                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Adventure Lamp, developed and published by Ryan Davis, is an indelibly cute puzzle platformer about hat physics. Yes, that's right.. hat physics. This is what differentiates the game from the multitude of other indie platformers in the Steam catalog.\n\n[h1]Simple Design in a Challenging Package[/h1]\n\nThe game captures your attention because the cuteness factor is turned all the way up to twelve. However, it manages to keep it because it is designed very simply but presents enough of a challenge. The majority of the 150 levels are short and are intended to be completed relatively quickly. As a result this generally means that you're never stuck on any one level for too long. There's more than a sufficient amount of content within the game to satisfy even the most content hungry gamer.\n\n[h1]It's All About The Hat[/h1]\n\nSeriously, the game is entirely about the hat. Every time you jump or bounce your hat leaves your head. You can also throw, toss and do whatever else you want to do with your hat to help you avoid all of the nasty pitfalls. Your hat is deadly. It will serve as a weapon to rid the screen of slimes. The slimes often generate very quickly meaning that every action that you take after losing your hat has to be taken that little bit quicker.\n\nHowever, despite the hat being your greatest ally there are a number of levels where that is just not the case. The more you lose your hat the worse the situation is for you. This provides a great little twist in a game that could be perceived as relatively straight forward otherwise.\n\n[h1]Graphics & Sound[/h1]\n\nPerhaps the most surprising thing about the game is the manner in which the atmosphere is presented. My initial thoughts were that I wouldn't want to live in this world and I wondered why the character is such a charming little individual given the darkness that surrounds him. The place is very gloomy and almost deathlike.  This is most noteworthy because it is in stark contrast with the remainder of the game including the sound. The sound is very cute which is in line with what I have come to expect from the game. As a result it seems like there is a real clash of atmosphere here. It doesn't really impact the game negatively but it is curious game design decision.\n\n[h1]Is it Steamified?[/h1]\n\nPartially. The game has Steam achievements, 13 in all, but it presently lacks trading cards. Hopefully cards are released in a future update.\n\n[h1]Verdict[/h1]\n\nI loved the cuteness of the game. I fell in love with the hat physics. The system was intelligently designed and gives the title a different selling point. I might balk a little at the price but that's because there are so many cheaper alternatives. But in all, Adventure Lamp is a really solid platformer that is worthy of your time if you are a fan of the genre.\n\nFor similar games and our popular giveaways (including hardware) please visit [url=http://www.steamified.com]Steamified[/url]",
